// THE PARTICLE, declared once.
//
// This is the layout of one element of the persistent particle state that
// Programs/Particles/ParticleSimulate.shader writes and Programs/Particles/ParticleBillboard.shader
// reads. It was declared independently in both of those files until Г4, and the drift had already
// started: Д26 gave Age.yzw a meaning in the simulation's copy and left the draw's copy a comment
// behind. A lane that means one thing in one file and nothing in the other is not yet a defect —
// both copies were still 64 bytes — but the next edit that changes a SIZE on one side only makes the
// draw pass read every particle from an offset the simulation never wrote to, and what that looks
// like in a frame is a badly tuned emitter rather than an error.
//
// THE THIRD STATEMENT OF THE SAME FACT IS IN C++: Graphic::System::kParticleStride
// (Engine/Graphic/Systems/Scene/Particles/ParticleGpuLayout.hpp) is what allocates and zeroes the
// state, in bytes, and it cannot be folded into this text. Tests/Engine/ShaderCacheKey compiles both
// stages for real and asserts the array stride the compiler produced against that constant, so the
// two sides now fail a test instead of agreeing by comment.
//
// A PLAIN STRUCT AND NOT THE STORAGE BLOCK ITSELF, because the two consumers deliberately disagree
// about both things a block declares. The simulation binds it read-write at slot 0 — a compute pass
// binds by the argument handed to SetStorageBuffer and never consults reflection — and the draw
// reads it read-only at slot 1, where the graphics descriptor write uses the resource's own slot.
// One text for what must agree; one line each for what must not.
//
// FIELDS ARE APPENDED, NEVER INSERTED, and kParticleStride is appended with them.

#ifndef PARTICLE_STATE_GLSLH
#define PARTICLE_STATE_GLSLH

struct Particle
{
    vec4 PosSize; // xyz = world position, w = current size
    vec4 Color;   // rgba = current colour (a folds in the over-life alpha; 0 => dead/invisible)
    vec4 VelLife; // xyz = velocity, w = lifetime (<= 0 => dead / unspawned)
    // x = age in seconds. yzw are the SIMULATION's local-space offset from the emitter, written only
    // while the emitter simulates in local space; the draw pass must not read or repurpose them.
    vec4 Age;
};

#endif // PARTICLE_STATE_GLSLH
